    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"Every displayed source presents the same severe and unresolved version of policy debate.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_a97d015a311e7316\",\"quote\":\"On the Scottish national interest, I totally respect the Scottish National party’s position: it has always campaigned for independence, because that is what the SNP does. However, does the right hon. Gentleman agree that in the 2017 general election, the majority—56%—of voters in Scotland voted for parties that were committed to delivering on Brexit? The percentage of the vote for…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_756007eb7e3268a8\",\"quote\":\"While we are talking about sport, may I say that this does not involve only rugby players? There is now evidence that footballers, particularly those heading the ball, suffer sustained brain injuries. It used to be interpreted as dementia, but it is a lot more serious than that. Has my hon. Friend had any discussions with the Football League about that?\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"whole_packet_no_support\",\"mechanism\":\"The evidence presents diverse policy debates across different contexts (Brexit, Scottish independence, football injuries).\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim falsely asserts a uniform presentation of policy debate, ignoring the varied and specific arguments presented in the sources.\",\"counterconditions\":\"\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The claim makes a sweeping generalization about the presentation of policy debate across multiple sources, which is unsupported by the evidence. The sources cover distinct policy areas and arguments, demonstrating the claim's inaccuracy.\"}",
